  "id": "deprivation-index",
  "term": "deprivation index",
  "definition": "A deprivation index is a combined measure that brings together multiple indicators of disadvantage to reflect deprivation more broadly than income alone. In this source, it is described for urban settings using non-income domains such as healthcare, education, housing, basic services, and infrastructure to represent the multidimensional nature of urban poverty.",
